" listen neste gang du starter på nytt <app>Diskbruksanalyse</app>."

#. (itstool) path: info/desc
#: C/scan-home.page:28
msgid "Scan all of your personal files that are on your computer."
msgstr "Skann alle dine personlige filer som ligger på datamaskinen din."

#. (itstool) path: page/title
#: C/scan-home.page:32
msgid "Scan your <file>Home</file> folder"
msgstr "Skann din <file>Hjem</file>-mappe"

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/scan-home.page:34
msgid ""
"The <file>Home</file> folder is where most files are located for most users "
"because default settings are often set to save or copy files into "
"subdirectories within it. This includes downloads from the internet, "
"documents which you work on and photos from your camera. Normally, one "
"<file>Home</file> folder exists for each user on the computer."
msgstr ""
"Mappen <file>Hjem</file> er der de fleste brukerne lagrer de fleste filene "
"sine, fordi standardinnstillingene ofte er satt til å lagre eller kopiere "
"filer til undermapper i den. Dette inkluderer nedlastinger fra internett, "
"dokumenter du jobber med og bilder fra kameraet. Normalt finnes det én "
"<file>Hjem</file>-mappe per bruker på datamaskinen."

#. (itstool) path: item/p
#: C/scan-home.page:42
msgid ""
"Select your <gui>Home Folder</gui> in the list of <gui>Devices &amp; "
"Locations</gui>."
msgstr ""
"Velg din <gui>Hjemmemappe</gui> fra listen over <gui>Enheter &amp; "
"steder</gui>."

#. (itstool) path: info/desc
#: C/scan-remote.page:28
msgid "Scan a folder remotely from your computer."
msgstr "Skann en mappe eksternt fra datamaskinen din."

#. (itstool) path: page/title
#: C/scan-remote.page:32
msgid "Scan a remote folder"
msgstr "Skann en fjernmappe"

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/scan-remote.page:34
msgid ""
"<app>Disk Usage Analyzer</app> can scan storage devices which are accessible"
" remotely. To scan the whole file system or any specific folder remotely:"
msgstr ""
"<app>Diskbruksanalyse</app> kan skanne lagringsenheter som er tilgjengelige "
"eksternt. For å skanne hele filsystemet eller en bestemt mappe eksternt:"

#. (itstool) path: item/p
#: C/scan-remote.page:40
msgid ""
"If you have scanned the remote file system before, select it under "
"<gui>Remote Locations</gui> in the list of <gui>Devices &amp; "
"Locations</gui>."
msgstr ""
"Hvis du har skannet filsystemet på en fjern enhet før, velg det under "
"<gui>Fjern steder</gui> i listen <gui>Enheter &amp; steder</gui>."

#. (itstool) path: item/p
#: C/scan-remote.page:45
msgid ""
"If you have connected to the remote file system before but not scanned it, "
"select the remote file system from the list."
msgstr ""
"Hvis du har koblet til et eksternt filsystem tidligere, men ikke skannet "
"det, velg det eksterne filsystemet fra listen."

#. (itstool) path: item/p
#: C/scan-remote.page:49
msgid ""
"If you have not connected to the remote file system before, enter the URL "
"into the <gui>Enter server address…</gui> field under <gui>Connect to "
"Server</gui>. It will normally have a protocol, followed by a colon and two "
"slashes, that looks different depending on the <link xref=\"help:gnome-"
"help/nautilus-connect#types\">protocol</link> that you are using."
msgstr ""
"Hvis du ikke har koblet til det eksterne filsystemet før, skriv inn URL-en i"
" feltet <gui>Skriv inn serveradresse</gui> under <gui>Koble til "
"server</gui>. Det vil normalt ha et protokollnavn, etterfulgt av kolon og to"
" skråstrek, som varierer avhengig av <link xref=\"help:gnome-help/nautilus-"
"connect#types\">protokollen</link> du bruker."

#. (itstool) path: item/p
#: C/scan-remote.page:55
msgid ""
"Click <gui>Connect</gui> to continue; you may be asked for more details, "
"like a password and username, before the scan will commence."
msgstr ""
"Klikk <gui>Koble til</gui> for å fortsette; du kan bli bedt om flere "
"detaljer, som passord og brukernavn, før skanningen starter."

#. (itstool) path: item/p
#: C/scan-remote.page:59
msgid "Select a folder if you do not want to scan the complete file system."
msgstr "Velg en mappe hvis du ikke vil skanne hele filsystemet."

